{"content":[{"c":["HAZAR-SUSAH, HAZAR-SUSIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City assigned to Simeon within the territory allotted to Judah for an inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.5","r":"Josh.19.5","rawR":"Josh.19.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.5","value":"Josh.19.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:5"},"); alternately called Hazar-susim (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.31","r":"1Chr.4.31","rawR":"1Chr.4.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.31","value":"1Chr.4.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:31"},"). Solomon probably used it as a transfer point for horses brought from Egypt for sale to the Hittites and Syrians, as suggested by its name, meaning “horse station.” Hazar-susah has been identified with Sbalat Abu Susein, east of the Wadi Far’ah."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HazarSusahHazarSusim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 19:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.5","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.5","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.31","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.31","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"213a9ecaae3fedbc17c83a5f4eadce60ea98d754b36c1682d01664eedd015a45","sourceItemName":"HazarSusahHazarSusim","sourceItemOrder":178,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"HazarSusahHazarSusim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hazar-Susah, Hazar-Susim","title":"Hazar-Susah, Hazar-Susim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}